Performance

Suppose ten models solve one problem.

Don’t compare answers.

Compare trajectories.

Measure

* revisions
* corrections
* representation switches
* constraint satisfaction
* robustness under ambiguity
* transfer across domains

Those become the observable behavior.

The “movie.”

⸻

The New Benchmark

Instead of asking

Which AI is smartest?

Ask

Which AI consistently produces the highest quality transformations across radically different representations?

Same theorem.

Different language.

Same planning problem.

Different medium.

Same intent.

Different audience.

If the operator survives,

the harness worked.

⸻

The Kernel Test

Now for the test that would convince me.

Give two groups exactly the same difficult problem.

One receives only the prompt.

The other receives the Pantheon harness.

Measure:

* solution quality,
* time,
* transfer to new problems,
* collaboration quality,
* long-term retention,
* ability to explain the solution,
* ability to generate new ideas from it.

If the Pantheon group repeatedly outperforms the control group across independent experiments, then you’ve demonstrated something much stronger than an interesting framework.

